      "source_contract_caveat": "Classic START zero is documented stop, not the L010/L011 explicit cursor-reset contract. MODE4 independently says each START converts the entire selected sequence exactly once. Fresh owned mode/configuration after stop is a software reuse argument, not proof of instantaneous analog cutoff or result-drain timing."
    },
    "implementation": {
      "single_irq": "MODE0 EOC plus OVW error",
      "scan_irq": "MODE4 EOS plus OVW error; do not enable per-slot EOC",
      "terminal_observation": "Single: EOC and START=0. Scan: EOS and START=0. OVW wins over completion. Use finite synchronous finalization once a completion event is retained.",
      "acknowledgment": "Typed ICR clears EOC/EOS/OVW and preserves EOA/WDTL/WDTH/WDTR; READY is status only.",
      "reuse_inference": "START=0 is documented stop. With EN disabled/reinitialized, all used mode/sequence fields freshly programmed and owned flags cleared, MODE4 documents a full finite sequence from the next start. Explicit sequence-cursor reset and analog drain timing are not claimed.",
      "inherited_state_rejection": "Before async ownership mutation, reject active external triggers, watchdog monitor/IRQ, EOA IRQ, accumulation and implemented DMA request enables; preserve inactive watchdog selection/thresholds and unrelated status.",
      "shared_analog": "Preserve live BGREN and retain its gate on F030/A030/F020/F003. F002 reserves BGREN/TSEN. L031/R031/W031/L052/L083 reserve BGREN and retain the existing exclusive ADC reference/source contract."
