  "lifecycle": {
    "ownership": "Typed IRQ binding and per-instance AtomicWaker/active/fault state; no caller buffer pointer in ISR or DMA.",
    "event_handoff": "Handler filters active owner and enabled pending owned source, masks the owned event(s), retains status and wakes. Task registers waker before final status check.",
    "result_commit": "Stage retained results locally, verify terminal state and owned mask/ack, then commit the entire output without an await; errors/cancellation leave output unchanged.",
    "cancellation": "Finite local mask/stop/disable/clear readbacks. Success permits fresh initialization. A failed required readback latches Faulted across mode changes and reconstructed owners until chip reset.",
    "interrupt_containment": "Normal cancellation leaves NVIC enabled. Emergency IRQ disable is allowed only on the metadata-proven dedicated line after failed owned masking.",
    "forgotten_future": "No borrowed pointer survives in ISR state, but forgetting skips cleanup and makes no quiescence promise. Every later operation repairs stopped/configured state.",
    "deadline": "Config.timeout bounds synchronous poll attempts only. Caller composes ordinary with_timeout/select using a functioning time/wake source."
  },
